<section class="ref-group"><h2>Battles <span class="n">23</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-haliartus"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Haliartus</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 395 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Haliartus was fought in 395 BCE outside the Boeotian city of Haliartus at the start of the Corinthian War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-coronea-394-bc"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-coronea-394-bc.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Coronea (394 BC)</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 394 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Coronea of 394 BCE was fought in Boeotia during the Corinthian War between a Spartan army under King Agesilaus II, newly returned from Asia, and a…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-allia"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Allia</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · c. 390 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Allia was fought around 390 BCE, or 387 BCE by Greek reckoning, near the River Allia north of Rome, where a Gallic army under Brennus routed the Romans.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-elleporus"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Elleporus</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 389 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Elleporus was fought in 389 BCE in southern Italy between Dionysius I of Syracuse and the Italiote League of Greek cities led by Croton.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tegyra"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Tegyra</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 375 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Tegyra was fought in 375 BCE near Orchomenus in Boeotia, when the Theban commander Pelopidas, leading the Sacred Band and a small force of cavalry, met a…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leuctra"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-leuctra.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Leuctra</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 371 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Leuctra was fought in Boeotia in 371 BCE between Thebes and its Boeotian allies under Epaminondas and a Spartan army under King Cleombrotus I.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-cynoscephalae-364-bce"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-cynoscephalae-364-bce.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Cynoscephalae (364 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 364 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Cynoscephalae in 364 BCE was fought in Thessaly between a Theban-led army under Pelopidas and Alexander, tyrant of Pherae.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-mantinea-362-bce"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Mantinea (362 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 362 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Mantinea was fought in Arcadia in 362 BCE between Thebes under Epaminondas, with its Arcadian and other allies, and a coalition of Sparta, Athens…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-guiling"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-guiling.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Guiling</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 354–353 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Guiling was fought in 354 or 353 BCE during the Warring States period.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-crocus-field"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-the-crocus-field.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Crocus Field</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 352 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Crocus Field was fought in Thessaly in 352 BCE during the Third Sacred War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-maling"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-maling.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Maling</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 342 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Maling was fought in 342 BCE between the State of Qi and the State of Wei, which had attacked Han.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-chaeronea-338-bce"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-chaeronea-338-bce.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Chaeronea (338 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 338 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Chaeronea was fought in Boeotia in August 338 BCE between Philip II of Macedon and an alliance led by Athens and Thebes.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-granicus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-the-granicus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Granicus</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 334 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Granicus was fought in 334 BCE at the Granicus River in northwestern Anatolia, the first major victory of Alexander the Great over the Persian satraps.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-issus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-issus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Issus</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 333 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Issus was fought in 333 BCE near the Gulf of Issus in south-eastern Anatolia between Alexander the Great and Darius III.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gaugamela"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-gaugamela.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Gaugamela</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 331 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Gaugamela was fought in 331 BCE in northern Mesopotamia between Alexander the Great and the Achaemenid king Darius III.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pandosia"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Pandosia</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 331 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Pandosia was fought in 331 BCE near the town of Pandosia in Bruttium, southern Italy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-jaxartes"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Jaxartes</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 329 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Jaxartes was fought in 329 BCE on the Syr Darya, near the newly founded Alexandria Eschate, between Alexander the Great and Saka nomads from beyond…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-hydaspes"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-the-hydaspes.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Hydaspes</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 326 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Hydaspes was fought in 326 BCE on the banks of the Hydaspes (Jhelum) in the Punjab between Alexander the Great and the Indian king Porus.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-amorgos"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-amorgos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Amorgos</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 322 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Amorgos was a naval battle fought in 322 BCE near the island of Amorgos during the Lamian War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-crannon"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Crannon</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 322 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Crannon was fought in 322 BCE in Thessaly between the Macedonian armies of Antipater and Craterus and the Greek allies led by Athens and the Aetolians.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-caudine-forks"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-the-caudine-forks.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Caudine Forks</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 321 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Caudine Forks in 321 BCE was a Roman disaster of the Second Samnite War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gaza-312-bce"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Gaza (312 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 312 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Gaza was fought in 312 BCE between Demetrius, son of Antigonus I, and the forces of Ptolemy I and Seleucus.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ipsus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/battle-of-ipsus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Ipsus</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 301 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Ipsus was fought in 301 BCE in Phrygia between Antigonus I and his son Demetrius on one side and a coalition of Seleucus I, Lysimachus and Cassander on…</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Sieges <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-pelium"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/siege-of-pelium.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Pelium</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 335 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Pelium was fought in 335 BCE when Alexander the Great attacked the Illyrian king Cleitus at the fortress of Pelion on the western border of Macedon.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/alexanders-siege-of-tyre"><span class="enc-name">Alexander's siege of Tyre</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 332 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">Alexander's siege of Tyre was the siege of the Phoenician island city of Tyre by Alexander the Great in 332 BCE.</span></a></li></ul></section>
