43–290 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Samnite Wars were three wars fought between the Roman Republic and the Samnites of the southern Apennines between 343 and 290 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/latin-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/latin-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Latin War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 340–338 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Latin War of 340–338 BCE was fought between Rome and its former allies of the Latin League, joined by the Campanians and Volsci.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-alexander-the-great"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/wars-of-alexander-the-great.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Wars of Alexander the Great</span><span class="enc-type">War · 336–323 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Wars of Alexander the Great were the campaigns fought by Alexander III of Macedon between 336 and 323 BCE, first to secure Greece and then against the Achaemenid…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/second-samnite-war"><span class="enc-name">Second Samnite War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 326–304 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Second Samnite War was fought between the Roman Republic and the Samnites from 326 to 304 BCE for control of Campania and central Italy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/lamian-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lamian-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Lamian War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 323–322 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Lamian War was a revolt of Athens, the Aetolian League and other Greek states against Macedonian rule after the death of Alexander the Great in 323 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-diadochi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/wars-of-the-diadochi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Wars of the Diadochi</span><span class="enc-type">War · 323–281 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Wars of the Diadochi were the conflicts fought between Alexander the Great's generals, the Diadochi or successors, for control of his empire after his death…</span></a></li></ul></section>
